Great. Before touching RTL, let's do what a design review would do: define the DMA behavior completely on paper.

Step 1: Define DMA Interface

The DMA should only know about configuration and status.

Inputs from reg_block
input  logic       clk;
input  logic       reset_n;

input  logic       enable;
input  logic [7:0] mode;
Output to reg_block
output logic [6:0] status;
Step 2: Define STATUS Encoding

Let's freeze this now.

STATUS[0] = BUSY
STATUS[1] = DONE
STATUS[2] = ERROR
STATUS[6:3] = RESERVED

Examples:

BUSY  = 0000001 = 0x01
DONE  = 0000010 = 0x02
ERROR = 0000100 = 0x04
Step 3: Define MODE Encoding

Keep it very simple.

MODE = 0x00  -> Normal Transfer

MODE = 0xFF  -> Error Transfer

Everything else:

Reserved for future use
Step 4: Define State Machine

I would use 4 states.

           +------+
           | IDLE |
           +------+
               |
               | enable=1
               v

           +------+
           | BUSY |
           +------+
               |
          5 clocks
               |
         +-----+-----+
         |           |
         |           |
 mode=00 |           | mode=FF
         v           v

      +------+   +-------+
      | DONE |   | ERROR |
      +------+   +-------+
